3.10. Ensemble Methods
3.10.1. Soft Voting Ensemble
Soft voting combines predictions from multiple base models via probability averaging [31]. The ensemble com-
bines Random Forest, XGBoost, Extra Trees, and SVM. Soft voting produces more stable predictions than hard
voting because it retains the confidence information encoded in predicted probabilities, allowing complementary
learners to contribute proportionally to their certainty.
3.10.2. Stacking Ensemble
Stacked generalization [23] trains a Level-1 meta-learner on out-of-fold probability vectors produced by Level-0
base models. In the proposed architecture, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost, and Random Forest serve as Level-0
learners, and Logistic Regression serves as the Level-1 meta-learner. The two-layer design is illustrated in Figure
4. Stacking exploits the complementary strengths of heterogeneous base learners by learning optimal combination
weights at the meta-level, in contrast to voting which relies on fixed averaging weights.
10
Figure 4: Two-layer Stacking Ensemble architecture.
3.10.3. Additional Ensemble Combinations
Four extended ensemble combinations are examined, each pairing learners with complementary inductive biases.
LightGBM [22], CatBoost [33], and AdaBoost [32] provide the boosting components in these combinations. The
combinations are: Random Forest + LightGBM, Extra Trees + LightGBM, Extra Trees + CatBoost, and Random
Forest + AdaBoost.
