4.5.1. Statistical Significance Testing
Model comparison is performed using three complementary statistical tests. The DeLong test [34] compares
areas under two correlated ROC curves. McNemar’s test compares paired binary classification outcomes. Paired
bootstrap confidence intervals with 2,000 resamples estimate the sampling distribution of metric differences.
Applied to the Stacking Ensemble and the strongest baseline Gradient Boosting, the results are as follows. The
```
DeLong test yields p = 0.786 (Stacking ROC-AUC = 0.7655 vs GB ROC-AUC = 0.7775), indicating no signif-
```
icant difference in ranking performance. McNemar’s test yields p = 0.2386. The paired bootstrap yields ∆F1
= −0.0012 with a 95% CI of [−0.0481, 0.0526]. Because the confidence interval includes zero and the p-values
are well above 0.05, it is concluded that the Stacking Ensemble does not statistically significantly outperform the
simpler Gradient Boosting model or Logistic Regression on this dataset.
